WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.340
Welcome back, champ!

2
00:00:04.340 --> 00:00:12.780
Last time: a quarter turn = 90°

3
00:00:12.780 --> 00:00:19.180
Unit 3 · Chapter 5 · the last one!

4
00:00:19.180 --> 00:00:25.350
Chapter 5 · Draw With Math

5
00:00:25.350 --> 00:00:34.440
Draw with commands, like a programmer!

6
00:00:34.440 --> 00:00:43.440
Meet Kachhu, the robot turtle

7
00:00:43.440 --> 00:00:49.520
"Kachhu, draw a square!"

8
00:00:49.520 --> 00:00:54.250
Kachhu doesn't move…

9
00:00:54.250 --> 00:01:00.690
Why didn't Kachhu draw? Think!

10
00:01:00.690 --> 00:01:12.900
He only understands tiny commands

11
00:01:12.900 --> 00:01:17.850
Command = one clear instruction

12
00:01:17.850 --> 00:01:28.290
forward 4 → walk 4 steps, draw a line

13
00:01:28.290 --> 00:01:36.100
The number = how many steps

14
00:01:36.100 --> 00:01:50.260
turn right 90 → spin a quarter turn

15
00:01:50.260 --> 00:01:55.690
Forward draws. Turning spins.

16
00:01:55.690 --> 00:02:04.920
A square: 4 equal sides, 4 square corners

17
00:02:04.920 --> 00:02:13.420
forward 4, turn right 90 · side 1

18
00:02:13.420 --> 00:02:25.880
Again… side 2. Again… side 3

19
00:02:25.880 --> 00:02:37.170
Side 4 · back to the start!

20
00:02:37.170 --> 00:02:46.010
4 times: forward 4, turn right 90

21
00:02:46.010 --> 00:02:50.260
8 lines… that's a lot!

22
00:02:50.260 --> 00:03:01.950
repeat 4 [forward 4, turn right 90]

23
00:03:01.950 --> 00:03:07.470
Repeat = a loop

24
00:03:07.470 --> 00:03:17.980
Commands in order = a tiny program!

25
00:03:17.980 --> 00:03:26.300
Bigger square? Which number changes?

26
00:03:26.300 --> 00:03:34.490
forward 4 → forward 8

27
00:03:34.490 --> 00:03:45.690
Keep turn right 90 and repeat 4

28
00:03:45.690 --> 00:03:54.920
4 sides × 4 steps = 16 steps

29
00:03:54.920 --> 00:04:01.380
4 sides × 8 steps = 32 steps

30
00:04:01.380 --> 00:04:10.850
Rectangle: long side 6, short side 3

31
00:04:10.850 --> 00:04:18.640
forward 6, turn, forward 3, turn

32
00:04:18.640 --> 00:04:28.520
repeat 2 [forward 6, turn, forward 3, turn]

33
00:04:28.520 --> 00:04:35.330
How many steps in total?

34
00:04:35.330 --> 00:04:41.140
6 + 3 + 6 + 3 = 18 steps

35
00:04:41.140 --> 00:04:51.740
Plus sign · new command: back

36
00:04:51.740 --> 00:04:59.190
forward 2, back 2, turn right 90

37
00:04:59.190 --> 00:05:04.230
repeat 4 → 4 arms → a plus sign!

38
00:05:04.230 --> 00:05:09.680
Uh-oh! A broken square

39
00:05:09.680 --> 00:05:22.170
Only 3 sides. How do you fix it?

40
00:05:22.170 --> 00:05:32.150
Fix: add one more forward 4

41
00:05:32.150 --> 00:05:45.890
Faces north · forward 2, right 90 · twice

42
00:05:45.890 --> 00:05:55.970
North → East → South

43
00:05:55.970 --> 00:06:02.370
Your turn: practice check

44
00:06:02.370 --> 00:06:12.570
Write commands: a square, 4 steps a side

45
00:06:12.570 --> 00:06:26.190
repeat 4 [forward 4, turn right 90]

46
00:06:26.190 --> 00:06:32.840
Square = repeat 4 [forward, turn right 90]

47
00:06:32.840 --> 00:06:36.040
Forward number = the size

48
00:06:36.040 --> 00:06:40.070
Forward draws. Turning spins.

49
00:06:40.070 --> 00:06:42.910
Commands in order = a tiny program

50
00:06:42.910 --> 00:06:55.660
Chapter 5 done · Unit 3 complete!

51
00:06:55.660 --> 00:07:02.460
Next: Quiz · Tap Finish
